35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The closeout files show steady, catalogue-style work outlasts flashy mechanism studies. I value that durability.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The rolls are empty. The technicians are gone. I cannot support a proposal needing hands we do not have.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The animal facility is accredited and staffed, but the glasshouses are full. Computing is free, though.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The grant buys less. The agency still covers computing, but the animal day rates have spiked.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,The overruns hit the breeding colonies hardest. I am worried about the biological timelines.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"Ryuji, that is a serious constraint. We must respect the staffing reality, even if it hurts.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,It is not just a constraint. It is a wall. I will not vote for a project that cannot be staffed.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"I agree with Ryuji. If the glasshouses are full, we cannot run the plant-based proposals.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,The financial data confirms it. The animal work is now the most expensive line item.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,This aligns with my findings. The biological delays are the biggest risk to the timeline.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,So we are looking for projects that are computationally heavy but biologically light? That seems prudent.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Exactly. The modelling posts are full of applicants. We have the brains, but not the hands.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,The computing agreement is a lifeline. We should prioritize the proposals that use it heavily.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,The purchasing power is skewed. We must choose the project that maximizes output per dollar.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I am concerned about the long-term impact. If the biology fails, the whole project stalls.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,Let us keep this in mind. We want a project that will still be useful in ten years.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I will vote for the proposal that matches our current staffing reality. No more, no less.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I will filter by facility availability. If the machines are free, the project is viable.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I will calculate the cost-effectiveness. The numbers will tell us the truth.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,I will look for the project with the least vulnerability to external biological delays.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
